1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,911
Platforms already use algorithms to judge us.

2
00:00:02,991 --> 00:00:07,300
AppealOS gives ordinary people a tireless digital advocate of their own.

3
00:00:07,600 --> 00:00:18,883
A rider, seller, creator, or developer can lose an account, income, or audience because of an automated fraud signal, an identity failure, an unexplained complaint, or a moderation mistake.

4
00:00:18,963 --> 00:00:27,133
Then the person is expected to reconstruct the allegation, the policy, the deadline, and the follow-up process through a contextless form.

5
00:00:27,213 --> 00:00:31,104
The affected person cannot see which facts or policies matter.

6
00:00:31,184 --> 00:00:38,187
Deadlines and supplement requests are easy to miss, and the same context must be rebuilt over and over.

7
00:00:38,267 --> 00:00:41,110
Rejection leaves no portable record for human escalation.

8
00:00:41,410 --> 00:00:45,565
AppealOS turns a platform suspension into an executable case.

9
00:00:45,645 --> 00:01:00,418
It reads the notice, identifies the allegation and the deadline, inspects only user-approved evidence, reconstructs a citation-backed fact timeline, compares the facts with a versioned policy profile, and compiles grounded claim units.

10
00:01:00,498 --> 00:01:11,930
After one scoped Appeal Mandate, the agent submits, handles one authorized supplement, tracks the response, and verifies a clear result: restored, rejected, or human escalation.

11
00:01:12,430 --> 00:01:18,370
Here is the live case workspace, running on Cloud Run. A MockDrop rider is suspended for abnormal location.

12
00:01:19,270 --> 00:01:29,950
AppealOS extracts the allegation, the incident window, and the deadline, and shows exactly three synthetic evidence artifacts: a delivery receipt, a GPS trace, and a device log.

13
00:01:30,850 --> 00:01:38,490
The user grants analysis consent first. Analysis means building the timeline and drafting claims. It does not disclose anything to the platform.

14
00:01:39,390 --> 00:01:46,900
Next, the agent compiles grounded claim units. Every claim carries artifact citations, a source span, and a confidence result.

15
00:01:47,800 --> 00:01:57,950
The user reviews one scoped Appeal Mandate: a single recipient, named claims, allowed evidence, one supplement cycle, polling, verification, and a seventy-two-hour expiry.

16
00:01:58,850 --> 00:02:02,990
Any new claim, new recipient, or new evidence class requires a new mandate.

17
00:02:03,890 --> 00:02:09,090
After one approval, the agent submits the initial appeal through a typed adapter with an idempotency key.

18
00:02:09,990 --> 00:02:14,040
MockDrop accepts the appeal and publishes a supplement request for the device log.

19
00:02:14,940 --> 00:02:23,820
Because the device log is already inside the mandate, AppealOS supplies it automatically, with no second user prompt. The account transitions from suspended to active.

20
00:02:24,720 --> 00:02:31,200
Every external write leaves a durable receipt. Submission, acknowledgement, supplement, and decision are distinct events.

21
00:02:32,100 --> 00:02:39,640
Replaying the supplement event produces no duplicate platform action, because the idempotency key and request hash are checked by deterministic code.

22
00:02:40,540 --> 00:02:47,900
AppealOS never equates approval text with restored access. Only after a direct account-status call returns active does it close the case.

23
00:02:48,800 --> 00:02:57,340
The user can then download a redacted, hash-consistent due-process audit export. The record excludes raw evidence, coordinates, keys, and tokens.

24
00:02:58,810 --> 00:03:04,690
Under the hood, the AppealOS UI and ADK runtime run on Cloud Run.

25
00:03:04,770 --> 00:03:12,912
Gemini handles structured notice extraction, evidence relevance, and grounded drafting. Deterministic code enforces deadlines, mandate scope, and idempotency.

26
00:03:12,992 --> 00:03:18,420
Firestore is the durable workflow authority. Cloud Storage holds encrypted synthetic evidence.

27
00:03:18,500 --> 00:03:26,000
Pub/Sub carries the supplement event from MockDrop back to the runtime, and Cloud Logging keeps redacted traces.

28
00:03:27,250 --> 00:03:30,400
Here is the deployed backend on Google Cloud.

29
00:03:30,400 --> 00:03:34,900
AppealOS and MockDrop run as separate Cloud Run services, each serving one hundred percent of traffic.

30
00:03:34,900 --> 00:03:38,900
The verified demo returned ACCOUNT_ACTIVE, with Gemini ready on Vertex AI

31
00:03:38,900 --> 00:03:42,400
and the request path logged end-to-end.

32
00:03:42,400 --> 00:03:50,645
AppealOS is a synthetic proof of concept. It never promises reinstatement, and every claim stays inside user-approved scope.

33
00:03:50,725 --> 00:03:54,442
One approval. One authorized supplement. One verified outcome.

34
00:03:54,522 --> 00:03:58,130
AppealOS: a digital advocate for an algorithmic world.
